_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:513:Raw types are `*const T` / `*mut T` (slice 24). Dereference/store use unary `*` and place assignment; `as` handles the decided reference/pointer and pointer/integer conversions, all gated as required by [OD98](../docs/decisions.md#od98). Pointer addresses do not carry integer provenance; every raw access requires typed validity/provenance/aliasing premises (Core Q3.7–Q3.11). Reference-derived pointers stay confined to the borrow, except explicit kept foreign retention with the receipt discipline ([OD64](../docs/decisions.md#od64), Core Q3.12). A write derived from shared &T remains forbidden ([OD112](../docs/decisions.md#od112)).
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:515:Slice 25 declares C bindings as `extern fn`, optionally `trusted extern fn`, explicit `with(...)`, mandatory semicolon and no body. `#[link_name = "symbol"]` and `#[export_name = "symbol"]` payload forms are recommendations (OPEN-15), not an inferred `extern "C" {…}` block. Direct calls only: foreign function values and `extern "C" fn` types are not admitted ([OD4](../docs/decisions.md#od4)). FFI-safe types exclude enums ([OD110](../docs/decisions.md#od110)); C structs cross by value at every size ([OD122](../docs/decisions.md#od122)). `kept` is decided, but marker placement, explicit call-only annotation and paired-ending source signatures are OPEN-23. Semantic validity obligations must not be replaced by inventing an `unsafe {…}` source block.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:601:Postfix `?`, value `while … else`, and postfix member `->` are explicitly described as removed in the [frozen grammar](../legacy/grammar/concrete.ebnf) and legacy syntax materials; **no specific deciding row in decisions.md was found for those three removals**. Their historical refusal is evidence, not an invented OD citation. **OPEN-25** recommends carrying the refusals forward and asks the owner to ratify them. Do not confuse postfix `->` with the retained function result arrow. Similarly this sheet does not treat block comments/exponents as an owner-decided removal without OPEN-1/5 approval.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:631:23. **OPEN-23 — Raw/FFI qualifiers and retention spelling (24/25).** Recommend `kept p: *mut T`, unmarked pointer parameter call-only by default, ptr-qualified raw APIs with a documented exception for decided read_owned(p), paired Kept receipt ending calls, extern fn without ABI-string blocks. Alternative: explicit `call_only` and `kept` markers on all pointer parameters, global raw operation names. Reason: Q3.12 decides kept/Kept, not every token position or qualification; OD64 confinement and OD13 move-out must remain visible.
_review/GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md:633:25. **OPEN-25 — Historical refusals without located deciding rows.** Recommend ratify refusal of postfix ?, value while…else and postfix ->; keep only function result ->. Alternative: reopen each as a separate language proposal. Reason: the frozen grammar documents removal, but no matching authoritative deciding anchor was found; attaching an unrelated OD would invent a decision.
