let_after_name = [\":\", type], \"=\", expr, \";\"
               | let_pattern_path_tail, \"{\", pattern_fields, \"}\", \"=\", expr, \";\" ;
let_pattern_path_tail = {\"::\", IDENT} ;
ghost_let     = \"ghost\", \"let\", [\"mut\"], IDENT, [\":\", type], \"=\", expr, \";\" ;''')
s=s.replace('| \"ghost\", let_head','| ghost_let')
s=s.replace('ghost let sharing ordinary let','ghost let restricted to a plain name binding')
s=s.replace('Whether an unqualified fieldless variant is also legal, char literal patterns, module-qualified destructuring heads, nested patterns and mixing "'`..` with named fields are **OPEN-17**.'"', '''Irrefutable enum lets and mutable pattern binders are retained ([PAT-10/11](../legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md#PAT-10)); the factored let path admits module-qualified struct and enum heads, subject to OPEN-17 exact path closure. Nested patterns remain deferred, and fields must be handled explicitly or through the decided ignore forms (OD25). Generic pattern paths such as "'`E::<T>::V` are accepted by the frozen parser but not established by that fact as a new decision: OPEN-17 must explicitly disposition them; the kernel above does not yet include their arguments. Char literal patterns and the precise payload-rest combination grammar remain OPEN-17.

**Wording conflict requiring clarification:** OD25/PAT-3 allow a “bare variant name” only for a fieldless variant; the chapter’s “No bare variant names” subsection requires enum qualification. “Bare” may mean no payload braces rather than no enum prefix. Retain qualified patterns in this proposed kernel, but do not declare an authoritative general refusal of unqualified fieldless variants without owner clarification. No nested-pattern admission is proposed.'"''')
s=s.replace('pattern_fields ;\\narm', 'pattern_fields ;\\narm')
