Also refuse exceptions/unwinding, capturing closures, trait objects/hidden dynamic dispatch, source macros/derive, derived equality, default and variadic functions, shadowing, implicit conversions and truthiness under the [binding refusal list](../docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#what-concrete-refuses) and [P16–P17](../docs/decisions.md#decided-project-refusals). Diagnostics should point to explicit match/error arms, named functions/context, static dispatch, reviewed generated source, written arguments and canonical numeric conversions as applicable. General comptime and broad `#[cfg]` remain refused pending the stated workload/proof/audit reopening conditions; they are not permanent refusals. `ptr::cmp` is refused by [OD37](../docs/decisions.md#od37) (use the sign of ptr::diff), and reference-to-reference casts by OD103. No new refusal is decided here.

`discard(e)` is an ordinary reserved builtin call, not a missing keyword statement: [builtin catalog](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md#builtin-functions), OD62/OD153. Its early availability at slice 3 is an explicit builtin-call exception before general calls at slice 5. Adding `discard expr;` would be a new spelling proposal, not a correction.
'"''' +s[b:]
s=s.replace('| contextual "'`spec`/`self`/attribute words vs IDENT |'"','| contextual "'`self`/attribute words vs IDENT |'"')
s=s.replace('spec at item start can dispatch before IDENT is legal there','spec/by/kept/Self proposed reserved; existing self remains contextual under OD90')
s=s.replace('| "'`let IDENT` binding vs struct destructuring |'"','| "'`let IDENT` binding vs struct/enum destructuring |'"')
s=s.replace('qualified heads OPEN-17','consume qualified path before field list; generic heads OPEN-17')
s=s.replace('| empty unit vs grouped expression |', '''| optional arm separator vs negative next pattern | FIRST/FOLLOW on "'`-` | require a comma after every arm in this proposal (OPEN-17); otherwise `x -1` can continue the previous expression or begin the next pattern |
| contextual kept vs parameter named kept | FIRST/FIRST if kept is IDENT | reserve kept under OPEN-3; if owner keeps it contextual, consume name once and dispatch on `:` versus the next parameter name |
| named generic trait head | semantic overacceptance, not FIRST/FIRST | impl prefix `<` versus named head is distinct; after parsing, refuse arguments on the trait in `impl Trait for Type` (OD148), and reject capability-only value types |
| empty unit vs grouped expression |'"''')
s=s.replace('one prefix parsed before statement dispatch, handed to loop or expression classifier', 'one prefix parsed before statement dispatch, handed to loop or expression classifier; suppress only the duplicate root attributed_postfix prefix, restoring it after a unary prefix or nested expression entry')
s=s.replace('parse assertion once; only grouped assertion admits by suffix; exact restriction OPEN-13','parse the complete contract expression once; retain whether its ROOT is grouping. Only then accept by on a grouped root. "'`(a) == b` has a binary root and cannot take by; exact annotated grammar remains OPEN-13'"')
s=s.replace('Precedence, low to high,', 'Cast-result postfix continuations are deliberately inherited from the frozen "'`cast_expr` production: `x as T.f()` operates on the completed cast, while `x.f() as T` selects the field first. This contextual continuation is not an additional global precedence level; its full grammar remains OPEN-8.'"\\n\\nPrecedence, low to high,')
s=s.replace('No wildcard,', 'No wildcard,')
s=s.replace('no wildcard, whole-module alias', 'wildcard already refused by [MOD-2](../legacy/docs/spec/modules.md#MOD-2), no whole-module alias')
# Replace recommendation lines individually, retaining IDs and original proposals except precise changes.
lines=s.splitlines()
for i,l in enumerate(lines):
 if l.startswith('1. **OPEN-1'): lines[i]=l.replace('to LF or EOF','to LF, CR or EOF').replace(' Confirm CR-only comment behavior separately.',' CRLF leaves LF as whitespace.')
 if l.startswith('3. **OPEN-3'): lines[i]=l.replace('use spec/by/kept contextually','reserve spec/by/kept/Self').replace('preserve explicit existing reservations','preserve explicit existing reservations and contextual self under OD90')
 if l.startswith('4. **OPEN-4'): lines[i]=l+' Q7.10 already approves the hosted grant table; only consolidation/transcription is outstanding there.'
 if l.startswith('5. **OPEN-5'): lines[i]=l.replace('no separators/suffixes','no separators; retain typed integer suffixes to preserve the approved Q6.2 example, with exact suffix grammar still for approval').replace('Reason: freeze','Reason: do not silently contradict "'`200u8` in the approved field example; freeze'"')
 if l.startswith('13. **OPEN-13'): lines[i]=l.replace('ghost let sharing ordinary let','name-only ghost let (CON-4)')
 if l.startswith('15. **OPEN-15'): lines[i]=l.replace('test functions parameterless, result u8','test functions already parameterless (STMT-10), result u8 (OD146 revised); do not reopen either')
 if l.startswith('17. **OPEN-17'): lines[i]='17. **OPEN-17 — Exact kept pattern/arm surface (9/10/16).** Recommend qualified enum patterns, "'`_` catch-all, integer/bool/char literals, OR patterns, named field renaming, whole-payload `{..}` and a mandatory comma after every arm. Keep irrefutable enum lets, mut applying to every binder, explicit field handling and the deferred status of nested patterns. Alternative: comma only after non-block arms, subject to FIRST/FOLLOW proof. Clarify OD25’s “bare” fieldless wording against the chapter’s qualification rule; explicitly disposition generic `E::<T>::V` and module-qualified let paths. Do not treat the frozen parser as authority for a new accepted form.'"'
 if l.startswith('20. **OPEN-20'): lines[i]=l.replace('named fields and puns, empty struct literal','explicit constructor field values (no expression puns); retain decided pattern punning and empty struct literals').replace('list/repeat arrays','nonempty list/repeat arrays (TYPE-7)').replace('Alternative: require all field labels/values, disallow puns and allow only constructor calls.','Alternative: retain expression puns.').replace('Reason: close historical conveniences','Reason: explicit values distinguish field labels from moved locals; close historical conveniences')
