('Aliases/constants','Agree','Agree','Agree','Keep.'),
('Imports','Agree','Agree; final dot; glob already refused','Final dot; no trailing comma','Keep final dot; wildcard refusal is settled, list punctuation remains open.'),
('Receivers','Agree','Only self/&self/&mut self; no self:T','Agree shorthand only','Keep shorthand as canonical receiver; typed self cannot add a second Destroy protocol. Separate proposal may remove dot calls.'),
('Proof syntax','Agree','Agree except name-only ghost','Parenthesized assert/assume only','Keep existing assert/assume forms and grouped-root by rule; fix ghost name restriction. Parenthesis unification is a separate owner proposal.'),
('Types/generics','Agree','Agree','Kind-separated caps; type/brand before cap','Keep kind-neutral argument candidate, but explicitly reject cap names as ordinary types; ordering already constrained by OD88.'),
('Attributes','Agree','Agree; test shape settled','Agree','Keep; test shape is not OPEN.'),
('Blocks','Agree conditional on mechanical expansion','Agree','All statements end ; or explicit return/grouping','Keep decided value behavior; grammar proof remains required. New semicolons would revise accepted syntax.'),
('Patterns/arms','Mandatory arm commas','Qualified only; settled fields; no nesting; mandatory commas','Qualified only; no trailing field commas; nonblock arm commas','Require every arm comma; retain decided fields/no nesting. Bare wording conflict remains explicit; generic heads need disposition.'),
('Statements','Agree','Agree','All typed lets; add discard statement','Keep inference proposal outside slice 0; discard(e) already ordinary builtin. Explicit types separately recommended for owner review.'),
('Borrows/defer','Agree','Agree','Agree','Keep restriction proposal; Q4.7 clause combination remains explicit question.'),
('Constructors','Explicit expression fields; keep pattern puns','No empty arrays/puns; empty structs kept','No puns/trailing commas','Change to explicit expression fields; retain pattern puns; reject empty array lists and retain empty structs.'),
('API/views','Agree','Agree','Agree','Keep; distinguish scalar ct_eq inventory and array/view extension; add slice-15 swap_at.'),
('Brands/fn contracts','Agree subject to separate binder/scope approvals','Agree','Agree','Keep proposals pending owner; no inferred approval from Core constructors.'),
('FFI','Owned kept H, default settled, no borrowed retention','Agree v1; reserve kept','Agree v1','Correct to full Q3.12; remaining qualification only is open.'),
('Concurrency','Agree','Agree','Agree','Keep model review before tokens.'),
('Historical refusals','? settled; ratify other two','? settled; refuse other two','Agree ratify all three','Exclude decided ?; ask only while…else and member ->.'),
]
s=(p/'GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md').read_text(); pos=s.index('\\nRecommendations follow')
t='\\n### Reviewer choices and v2 disposition\\n\\n“Agree” means agreement with v1, not approval by the owner. The named choices below are taken from final answer sections only. Codex/Kimi checked the repository; agy could not. All 25 original IDs are retained so narrowed questions remain traceable.\\n\\n| OPEN | Topic | Codex | Kimi | agy | v2 recommendation and reason |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n'
for i,r in enumerate(rows,1): t+='| '+str(i)+' | '+' | '.join(r)+' |\\n'
s=s[:pos]+t+s[pos:]; (p/'GRAMMAR_REVIEW.md').write_text(s)
findings=[
('C1','accepted','Kept takes owned H, never borrow-derived pointers; full Q3.12 options/note expressly says so. Corrected raw/FFI prose and OPEN-23.'),
('C2','accepted','Q3.12 already chooses "'`kept buf: H`, no marker = call-only; removed false open choices.'"'),
('C3','accepted','Q7.10 approves the complete hosted table/signatures; remaining work is transcription, not owner reapproval.'),
('C4','accepted','P16 and PHILOSOPHY permanently refuse postfix ?; OPEN-25 now covers only the other two historical forms.'),
('C5','accepted','With optional arm commas, - starts both subtraction continuation and the next negative pattern; require separators in the proposed grammar.'),
('C6','accepted','P16/P17 and binding refusal list cover defaults/macros/derive and conditional reopening of comptime/cfg; added statuses and diagnostic directions.'),
('K1','accepted','OD129 explicitly applies OD46 argument-based inference, otherwise explicit; removed both expected-enum-type claims.'),
('K2','partly','Approved Q6.2 field example contains 200u8, conflicting with a blanket ban; it does not specify a complete suffix grammar. OPEN-5 now retains that evidence and asks exact policy.'),
('K3','accepted','TYPE-7@2 requires at least one array-literal element; removed empty list alternative and reopened-empty-array claim. Zero-length repeat policy is not decided by this correction.'),
('K4','accepted','OD65 plus approved slice 1 already admit empty struct literals; OPEN-20 no longer asks their admission.'),
('K5','partly','Explicit fields/ignore forms are settled by OD25 and nested patterns are deferred. Qualification is complicated by OD25/PAT-3 “bare fieldless” wording versus the chapter’s no-bare subsection; flagged the conflict rather than inventing a final refusal.'),
('K6','accepted','PAT-10/11 explicitly include irrefutable enum lets and mutable binders; extended factored let path beyond one IDENT.'),
('K7','accepted','Parser.lean 1600–1616 accepts E::<T>::V; implementation is evidence only (OD150). OPEN-17 now explicitly asks disposition, without adding it as decided syntax.'),
('K8','accepted','CON-4 rationale says ghost destructuring unsupported; split ghost_let from ordinary destructuring syntax.'),
('K9','accepted','OD98 covers trusted reference-to-raw conversion; OD103 refuses reference casts; Q3.9 supplies expose/from_exposed. Corrected the blanket as claim.'),
('K10','partly','Information-flow row includes ct_eq in the secret surface; roadmap explicitly delays array/view ct_eq to 15, but does not spell every scalar overload. Added scalar inventory at 7 with overload closure still OPEN-21.'),
('K11','accepted','Approved slice 15 names swap_at; added slice/operation entry before later heap-view replacement.'),
('K12','accepted','OD47 fixes while syntax; missing while from a claimed complete reserved list creates lexical overlap. Added while.'),
('K13','accepted','Contextual kept can also be the parameter IDENT; optional marker has FIRST overlap. Added conflict and proposed reservation under OPEN-3.'),
('K14','accepted','TRAIT-9 interprets Self specially; MOD-1 restricts its scope. Added lexical disposition, with reservation proposed rather than invented.'),
('K15','accepted','MOD-2 refuses glob imports; OPEN-11 now limits its question to punctuation/list details.'),
('K16','accepted','STMT-10 parameterized-test reject example fixes parameterless shape; result u8 comes from revised OD146. Neither is reopened.'),
('K17','accepted','Same verified permanent ? refusal as C4.'),
('K18','accepted','Binding refusal list contains the named omissions; supplemented inventory, distinguishing grammar exclusions from checked refusals and conditional reopening.'),
('A1','rejected','discard is an ordinary builtin call discard(e), documented in TYPE catalog and syntax/statements examples, reserved as a declaration name by OD153. No missing discard keyword or discard expr statement; clarified slice-3 availability.'),
('A2','rejected','OD47 explicitly uses expr before until and restricted head for upper bound. until, not a following block, delimits the lower expression; no asserted { FIRST/FOLLOW conflict.'),
('A3','rejected','argument has one type candidate then optional + suffix; cap_name is not a competing alternative. The kind check is already explicit. No FIRST/FIRST merely because an IDENT can denote a cap.'),
('A4','partly','Optional parameters start < while a named head starts IDENT/cap token: no claimed FIRST conflict. But trait arguments must be refused under OD148; made the semantic filter explicit. Capability-only value types were already rejected in prose.'),
('A5','partly','Qualified/enum let paths were missing and are corrected. let mut S { x } is expressly supported by PAT-11; mut applies to binders, so that alleged error is rejected.'),
('A6','rejected','method_params alternatives start & and IDENT, so disjoint. self is tested only after IDENT; existing contextual prose already states this. Ordinary typed params start IDENT, not &.'),
('A7','rejected','Frozen EBNF cast_expr explicitly permits postfix continuations after cast targets; SYN-2 precedence does not establish their prohibition. Clarified cast-result continuation and left full ratification OPEN-8.'),
('A8','rejected','place_base alternatives start IDENT, (, *: disjoint. *(p.f) is generated by * + ( place ); the alleged excluded example is actually admitted. Checked-place validity remains OD121/OPEN-20.'),
('A9','partly','v1 already says consume attributes once and nested expr restores prefixes, so no newly demonstrated conflict. Added explicit suppression of only the duplicate root prefix; full expanded grammar remains uncertified.'),
('A10','partly','Need to parse the complete assertion before deciding whether its root is grouping. A look only at its first ( is insufficient. Clarified (a)==b versus grouped-root suffix; requiring all assertions parenthesized would be a new decision.'),
('A11a','rejected','OD86 permits return arms. return x;, is a return terminator followed by an arm separator, not two alternative semicolon parses; mandatory separator is now proposed for all arms.'),
('A11b','partly','Q4.7/Q9.5 use optional range and else clauses; the row does not expressly settle every no-range/else combination. OPEN-19 already exposes this; retained the question without inventing an acceptance.'),
('A11c','rejected','Citation-check request, not an established error: OD115 required total spec body, OD79 assert plus SPARK suffix, OD91 generic-cast parentheses, OD147 combined layout, OD128 => and OD153 builtin collisions all match v1. OPEN-25’s ? error is accepted separately (C4/K17).'),
]
out='# Grammar review changes — v1 to v2\\n\\nChecked 2026-11-08. C = Codex final six findings; K = Kimi final eighteen; A = agy final ten plus its numbered citation checklist (A11a–c). agy had no repository access. Every reported claim is dispositioned below; duplicate findings remain separate for traceability. OPEN preference disagreements are recorded for all reviewers in v2’s final table. No recommendation here approves a language change.\\n\\nEvidence keys: [decisions](../docs/decisions.md) governs; [full Core rows](../docs/archive/decisions-2026-11-05/core_rows.json) expand the approved options/notes; [patterns](../legacy/docs/spec/patterns.md), [types](../legacy/docs/spec/types.md), [contracts](../legacy/docs/spec/contracts.md), [syntax](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md), [statements](../legacy/docs/spec/statements.md), [modules](../legacy/docs/spec/modules.md), [traits](../legacy/docs/spec/traits.md), [frozen parser](../legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Parser.lean), [frozen EBNF](../legacy/grammar/concrete.ebnf), [slices](../ROADMAP.md#vertical-slices) and [refusals](../docs/PHILOSOPHY.md#what-concrete-refuses) were read as supporting evidence, with decisions taking precedence. Current Lean modules model semantic subsets and supply no complete source lexer/grammar certificate. No legacy code or gates were run.\\n\\n'
for k,status,reason in findings: out+=f'- **{k} — {status}:** {reason}\\n'
(p/'GRAMMAR_CHANGES.md').write_text(out)
