5:### 1. Value-block tails (`{ stmts; expr }`) and dual-mode `if` / `match` (`value_block_tails`)
14:### 2. Struct construction and pattern field punning (`field_punning`)
23:### 3. Overloaded `as` for numeric casts, pointer casts, trait conversions, and `borrow` delimiters (`as_cast_operator`)
32:### 4. Overloaded `*` for `Heap<T, A>` move-out (`*h`) vs. reference and raw pointer dereference (`heap_star_deref`)
44:### 5. Dual method-call syntax (`x.m()` / `(&x).m()`) alongside qualified calls (`Type::m(&x)`) (`postfix_method_syntax`)
55:### 6. Unparenthesized vs. parenthesized `assert` and `#[proof(...)]` vs. `assert(...) by ...` (`assert_and_proof_forms`)
66:### 7. First-class brands, `exists<brand A>`, `pack`, and `unpack` in Slice 19 (`first_class_brands`)
75:### 8. Function values (`fn(...) with(...) -> T`), indirect calls, and higher-order safety contracts in Slice 20 (`first_class_fn_values`)
86:### 9. Two different key-value syntax conventions in attributes (`attribute_syntax_split`)
95:### 10. Two module path separators: `.` in `import a.b.{x};` vs. `::` in expressions and types (`import_dot_separator`)
104:### 11. Both `OrderedMap` and `HashMap` as built-in language/compiler nominal types in Slice 23 (`dual_builtin_maps`)
113:### 12. Candidates that look redundant but should be KEPT (`KEEP` verdicts)

