text='# Simplification candidates — merged owner list\\n\\n2026-11-08. Sources: final sections of [Codex](simplify_codex.out), [Kimi](simplify_kimi.out), and [agy](simplify_agy.out). “ASK” normalizes “WORTH ASKING.” “not raised” means no verdict on that specific candidate in that reviewer’s simplification answer; broader KEEP comments are not manufactured into votes on every subproposal. Overlapping bundles are split where their verdicts or effects differ.\\n\\nAll anchors below were checked against the repository. Decisions govern over legacy prose and implementation. CHANGE means **recommend an owner-approved revision**, not a decision or permission to implement. Exact unapproved replacement spellings are marked ILLUSTRATIVE. Reasons are at most 60 words each; workload benefits are judgments, not measured results. No language changes have been made.\\n\\nOrdered first by cross-review agreement and owner importance, then actionable surface reductions, unresolved semantic changes, and confirmed KEEP distinctions. The three reviewers have not reviewed this merged artifact.\\n\\n'
for i,it in enumerate(items,1):
 text+=f\"## {i}. {it['title']}\\n\\n**Today (verified):** {it['today']}\\n\\n**Proposed change:** {it['proposal']} **Lost:** {it['lost']}\\n\\n**Verdicts:** Codex **{it['c']}**; Kimi **{it['k']}**; agy **{it['a']}**.\\n\\n**Merged: {it['rec']}.** {it['why']}\\n\\n**Grammar interaction:** {it['opens']}\\n\"
 if it['example']: text+='\\n"'```con'"\\n'+it['example'].strip()+'\\n"'```'"\\n'
 assert len(it['why'].split())<=60,(it['title'],len(it['why'].split()))
Path('_review/SIMPLIFY_MERGED.md').write_text(text)
