11:**LL(1) status.** The expression and declaration kernels below are factored for predictive parsing. There are unresolved surface choices, especially statement/value blocks and contextual words. This is not a claim that a complete grammar has passed a mechanical LL(1) check. Section 8 identifies the remaining conflicts and the decisions needed; it would be false to promise a fully checked LL(1) grammar before those choices are approved. No decided spelling is changed to hide a conflict.
15:EBNF: `=` defines; `|` separates alternatives; `[x]` is optional; `{x}` repeats; quoted text is a token; `ε` is empty. `IDENT`, `INT`, `FLOAT`, `CHAR`, `STRING`, `LABEL`, `EOF` are token classes. Quoted identifier-shaped attribute names are contextual token tests, **not** automatically reserved words. `List(X)` and `List1(X)` below are explicitly defined list expansions. No uppercase/lowercase path heuristic is permitted: [OD152](../docs/decisions.md#od152).
29:| 8 | assert/assume, ghost bindings, total specification functions, theorem attributes, tests |
46:| 25 | extern declarations, symbol/layout attributes, kept/Kept |
80:false fn for from ghost if impl import let match mod mut pub return
84:Explicit decisions: `from`/`until` [OD50](../docs/decisions.md#od50); `ghost` [OD81](../docs/decisions.md#od81); `Copy` [OD90](../docs/decisions.md#od90); the nine capabilities, including `Console`, [authority rule 13](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-02-authority), as revised by [Q7.11](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core). [OD73](../docs/decisions.md#od73) forbids reserved words in identifier positions, including import aliases and variant names. The entropy capability arrives at slice 6, but its **name is not supplied by that decision**: [stack/randomness decision](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-07-stack-randomness). Do not reintroduce the historical capability `Random` without approval.
86:Recommend reserving `spec`, `by`, `kept` and `Self` under OPEN-3 (add them to the proposed list above); `while` is the decided loop keyword (OD47). `Self` has special type meaning under [TRAIT-9](../legacy/docs/spec/traits.md#TRAIT-9), and is not an ordinary free type name. Recommended contextual words: `self`; attribute names `proof`, `may_not_terminate`, `requires`, `ensures`, `invariant`, `variant`, `test`, `repr`, `link_name`, `export_name`; repr arguments `C`, `packed`, `align`. `result` is a special bound name only inside ensures. These contextual statuses, where not expressly settled, are OPEN-3. `self`, `repr`, `packed`, `align` were expressly left unchanged by OD90, not newly reserved by it.
105:Decimal integers arrive at 0; other bases at 2; FLOAT at 26; STRING/CHAR at 16 (a reason STRING in an earlier annotation is metadata, not a runtime StaticStr feature). Leading-zero decimal integers are explicitly refused: [slice-0 surface](../docs/decisions.md#decided-slice0-surface-2026-11-06). The old forms are documented by [SYN-6](../legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#SYN-6). **OPEN-5**: approve lowercase base prefixes, no separators, float digit/point syntax and a minimal typed-integer suffix policy and boundary handling; the frozen lexer also accepted uppercase prefixes. The [approved Q6.2 field example](../docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-q6-2-fields) contains `200u8`. A blanket suffix refusal conflicts with that example; OPEN-5 recommends retaining typed integer suffixes, but their complete width/base/boundary grammar needs approval. The displayed INT production is the unsuffixed kernel, not a complete suffix grammar. No exponent notation, `1.`, `.5`, hex floats or special NaN/Inf literals are proposed.
107:Minus is an operator, not part of INT/FLOAT. Literal expected typing and range checking include negation ([OD31](../docs/decisions.md#od31), [OD63](../docs/decisions.md#od63), [OD138](../docs/decisions.md#od138)); an unconstrained literal is refused, not defaulted. Float literals round directly to their expected width; no lexical suffix is implied by that rule.
130:Cast-result postfix continuations are deliberately inherited from the frozen `cast_expr` production: `x as T.f()` operates on the completed cast, while `x.f() as T` selects the field first. This contextual continuation is not an additional global precedence level; its full grammar remains OPEN-8.
179:extern_param  = ["kept"], IDENT, ":", type ;
204:In `method_params`, the second `method_ident_tail` alternative is legal only when the consumed identifier is contextual `self`; the first is an ordinary typed parameter. Its contextual-token treatment is OPEN-3/12. A typed consuming receiver `self: T` versus bare `self` must not accidentally create a second independent Destroy protocol; [OD60](../docs/decisions.md#od60) chooses one consuming form.
